{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["For I will not give you of their land — and likewise it is written concerning Moav: אל תצר את מואב, and likewise concerning the children of Ammon: אל תצורם. All these warnings Moshe needed to make known now, lest their hearts grow faint, saying: If it is the will of the Holy One, blessed be He, to give us an inheritance, and the power is in His hand, why did He not dispossess for us these nations through whose land we have journeyed?! Therefore he made it known to them now that the Holy One, blessed be He, had no desire for this — for the Holy One, blessed be He, had given it to them, as is written in all of them." "For as a possession to Esav I have given Mount Seir; for as a possession to the children of Lot I have given Ar — and also concerning Ammon: כי לבני לוט נתתיה ירושה — for the honor of Avraham, for they were his kinsmen."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:12.224009736Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}